re it completes, especially if the Virtual Machine Platform feature isn't enabled. Windows 11 Home China — WSL2 requires virtualization features.\n\nLet me check things first:\n- `wsl --status` — shows if WSL is installed\n- `wsl -l -v` — lists distros\n\nLet me run these. Note that in Git Bash on Windows, `wsl.exe` should be accessible.\n\nIf WSL isn't installed, I'll run `wsl --install --no-launch` or with Ubuntu. The default `wsl --install` installs Ubuntu (latest LTS) automatically. Since this may need admin, I might need to elevate via PowerShell:\n`powershell -Command \"Start-Process wsl -ArgumentList '--install' -Verb RunAs\"` — this triggers a UAC prompt which the user must approve.\n\nAlso, installing Ubuntu via `wsl --install -d Ubuntu` downloads it. This can take a while (download ~100-300MB+). Also may require reboot.\n\nAlternatively, the Microsoft Store approach. But CLI is cleaner.\n\nLet me start by checking the state. I'll run both checks in parallel."}
