{"schema_version": "1.0", "session_id": "27241a16-fd92-4412-8e49-69dc477094e4", "team_id": "contest2026_286_hajiminanbeilvdou", "github_login": "Oliweitz", "tool": "claude-code", "seq": 48, "ts": "2026-09-12T08:10:12.981Z", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "tokens_in": 80, "tokens_out": 463, "role": "assistant", "thinking": "The output file is empty. The elevated installer completed but wrote nothing to the redirected output. Interesting — exit code 0 but no distro installed.\n\nLet me check the Windows optional features state. `Get-WindowsOptionalFeature` requires admin. I can check the registry instead (non-admin readable):\n\n- VirtualMachinePlatform: HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Windows\\OptionalFeatures\\... hmm, actually the state of features can be checked via:\n`reg query \"HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\...\"` — not straightforward.\n\nBetter: check if the VM platform is present: `bcdedit /enum {current}` needs admin. \n\nAlternative non-admin check: `systeminfo` shows Hyper-V requirements including \"Virtualization Enabled In Firmware\" and \"A hypervisor has been detected\". That's a great non-admin check! `systeminfo` output at the bottom has \"Hyper-V 要求\" (Hyper-V requirements) section showing:\n- 已在固件中启用虚拟化: 是/否 (Virtualization Enabled In Firmware)\n- 已检测到虚拟机监控程序 (A hypervisor has been detected)\n\nLet me run systeminfo with proper encoding. In Git Bash, systeminfo output is GBK. Let me pipe through PowerShell with UTF8 output, or just grep for the relevant lines with iconv.\n\nLet me run: `systeminfo 2>&1 | iconv -f GBK -t UTF-8 | grep -A 6 -i \"hyper\"`"}
