{"schema_version": "1.0", "session_id": "27241a16-fd92-4412-8e49-69dc477094e4", "team_id": "contest2026_286_hajiminanbeilvdou", "github_login": "Oliweitz", "tool": "claude-code", "seq": 73, "ts": "2026-09-12T08:14:32.765Z", "role": "tool", "tool_name": "<result>", "tool_call_id": "call_01_6XDMAzzlhYdrhnwN3kLH7180", "input": null, "output": "以下是可安装的有效分发的列表。\r\n使用“wsl.exe --install <Distro>”安装。\r\n\r\nNAME                            FRIENDLY NAME\r\nUbuntu                          Ubuntu\r\nUbuntu-26.04                    Ubuntu 26.04 LTS\r\nUbuntu-24.04                    Ubuntu 24.04 LTS\r\nUbuntu-22.04                    Ubuntu 22.04 LTS\r\nopenSUSE-Tumbleweed             openSUSE Tumbleweed\r\nopenSUSE-Leap-16.0              openSUSE Leap 16.0\r\nSUSE-Linux-Enterprise-15-SP7    SUSE Linux Enterprise 15 SP7\r\nSUSE-Linux-Enterprise-16.0      SUSE Linux Enterprise 16.0\r\nkali-linux                      Kali Linux Rolling\r\nDebian                          Debian GNU/Linux\r\nAlmaLinux-8                     AlmaLinux OS 8", "is_error": false}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "session_id": "27241a16-fd92-4412-8e49-69dc477094e4", "team_id": "contest2026_286_hajiminanbeilvdou", "github_login": "Oliweitz", "tool": "claude-code", "seq": 74, "ts": "2026-09-12T08:14:40.828Z", "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "tokens_in": 312, "tokens_out": 755, "role": "assistant", "thinking": "Key findings:\n1. **LxssManager service is NOT installed** (error 1060: 指定的服务未安装) — WSL core didn't actually get installed! The `wsl --install` claimed success but the service isn't there.\n2. Network works fine — online distro list retrieves fine.\n\nSo the first `wsl --install --no-launch --web-download` apparently did NOT complete the WSL core install. Maybe the UAC prompt was declined, or the MSI install failed silently. Yet exit code 0...\n\nWait — actually the LxssManager service might only be created after a reboot, or the MSI installed but the service isn't registered until reboot. Hmm. On Windows 11, the WSL core is delivered as a Store app / MSI \"Windows Subsystem for Linux\" — the LxssManager service comes from the \"Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux\" optional feature, which is a Windows feature enabled by DISM. If the feature was just enabled (pending reboot), the service won't exist until reboot.\n\nThat aligns with the RebootRequired registry key we found. The `wsl --install` flow:\n1. Enables Windows features: Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux + VirtualMachinePlatform → **requires reboot**\n2. Downloads & installs WSL kernel/store package\n3. Installs the distro\n\nSince LxssManager service doesn't exist yet → feature enablement is pending reboot → the whole WSL subsystem can't register distros yet.\n\nSo the path forward: **reboot is required**, then run `wsl --install -d Ubuntu` again (or the distro install will work after reboot).\n\nActually wait — distro registration on Windows 11 WSL 2.x: distros are registered via the wslservice (from the WSL Store package), not LxssManager... The new WSL (2.x) uses wslservice.exe (which we saw running as PID 39788 earlier!). Hmm, interesting — wslservice WAS running. But `wsl -l -v` says no distros.\n\nLet me check the WSL version installed: `wsl --version`. And check if the \"Windows Subsystem for Linux\" store app got installed. Let me query the appx packages: `powershell Get-AppxPackage *Linux*` — non-admin readable."}
